From 6835538d2b5f84b9d7a345fd0677449ab32991ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:41:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] A spell's missiles can trail a glowing ribbon, be drawn
 larger and spin flat

Arrows and a thrown axe were too thin to follow at night, and no spell effect in the game's data
fixed that (Corey's review; 14 missiles were tried for Bank Shot alone). SetMissileLook(spellId,
colour, width, seconds[, scale[, spin[, caster]]]) gives every missile of a spell a ribbon behind
it (additive, soft-edged, facing the camera, fading from the head back), a size and a flat spin
about its up axis, as a boomerang turns; with a caster's guid it's for that caster's next missile
of the spell alone, within half a second (a ricochet's new colour). A missile reads its look as it
flies and for a quarter second after, so a look set in the same moment as the cast still takes.
HasActionCombat() is 20.
